27:T72b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How far is Madinah from AlUla by road?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Madinah to AlUla is about 330 km by road, heading north through open desert — roughly a 3-hour drive."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long is the drive from Madinah to AlUla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The drive takes around 3 hours, making AlUla an easy heritage trip to add after visiting Madinah. Most travellers make one short stop for fuel, food, and prayer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I combine my Madinah Ziyarah with an AlUla heritage trip?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Many pilgrims travel from Madinah to AlUla after their Ziyarah to visit Hegra, Dadan, and the Old Town. We collect you from your Madinah hotel and can keep the car for the day so you tour the sites with your chauffeur."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is AlUla known for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AlUla is home to the UNESCO-listed Hegra (Mada'in Salih), Dadan, AlUla Old Town, dramatic rock formations like Elephant Rock, and the Winter at Tantora festival — one of Saudi Arabia's leading heritage destinations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What vehicle is best for the Madinah to AlUla drive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A sedan suits 1–3 travellers with light luggage, while a GMC Yukon SUV or Hyundai Staria van is more comfortable for families and groups with bags on the desert drive."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is a taxi from Madinah to AlUla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The fare depends on your vehicle and group size, and whether you keep the car for the day. We confirm one fixed price on WhatsApp before booking — no surge, no hidden fees."}}]}1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-[#FAFAF7] text-[#1C1C1C]","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"_